!.env.example

# Mukul's original certificate documents (~11MB). Source material the site
# never reads — the web copies it actually serves live in `public/certificates`
# and ARE committed. Keep this ignore and that inclusion together: dropping
# `public/certificates` would break the Certifications section.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. Unanchored, this pattern matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, and Git on Windows is case-insensitive
# by default — so plain `Certificates/` also ignored `public/certificates`,
# silently excluding all 15 files the site actually serves. Anchored, it
# matches only the folder at the repository root.
/Certificates/
